        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 377.1,
          "end": 379.23,
          "en": "is related to our chart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 379.23,
          "end": 383.31,
          "en": "This chart widget in the end renders a container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 383.31,
          "end": 386.283,
          "en": "that has a width set to double infinity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 387.3,
          "end": 391.11,
          "en": "Now I'll get back to what exactly the problem with that is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 391.11,
          "end": 393.18,
          "en": "but in a nutshell, the problem is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 393.18,
          "end": 395.4,
          "en": "with this width setting here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 395.4,
          "end": 397.65,
          "en": "this container simply tries to take up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 397.65,
          "end": 400.32,
          "en": "as much width as it can get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 400.32,
          "end": 402.72,
          "en": "only restricted by the parent widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 402.72,
          "end": 404.07,
          "en": "in which this container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 404.07,
          "end": 407.67,
          "en": "so in which this chart in the end, is included.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 407.67,
          "end": 410.88,
          "en": "The problem with the chart being inside of a row now is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 410.88,
          "end": 414.3,
          "en": "that the row also has a width of infinity,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 414.3,
          "end": 417.21,
          "en": "so it tries to get as much width as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 417.21,
          "end": 418.40999999999997,
          "en": "And if you have a child",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 418.40999999999997,
          "end": 420.99,
          "en": "that tries to get as much width as it can get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 420.99,
          "end": 423.36,
          "en": "and you have a parent that tries to get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 423.36,
          "end": 425.25,
          "en": "as much width as it can get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 425.25,
          "end": 427.05,
          "en": "you get an error because Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 427.05,
          "end": 429.873,
          "en": "is not able to display a UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 431.07,
          "end": 432.06,
          "en": "To work around that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 432.06,
          "end": 435.03,
          "en": "you should wrap the chart also in expanded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 435.03,
          "end": 437.13,
          "en": "which is basically always the solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 437.13,
          "end": 439.74,
          "en": "whenever you have widgets nested into each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 439.74,
          "end": 441.633,
          "en": "that don't work together like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 442.77,
          "end": 444.09,
          "en": "And it should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 444.09,
          "end": 446.553,
          "en": "So if you save this and force a reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 447.69,
          "end": 451.14300000000003,
          "en": "you now see that indeed the chart sits next to the list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 452.1,
          "end": 455.67,
          "en": "And with that, we now got a UI that makes way more sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 455.67,
          "end": 458.55,
          "en": "because now this UI works here on landscape,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 458.55,
          "end": 461.01,
          "en": "but it also works on portrait mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 461.01,
          "end": 463.5,
          "en": "And you see that as I switch between those modes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 463.5,
          "end": 465,
          "en": "the UI gets updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 465,
          "end": 467.85,
          "en": "and gets adjusted to the available width.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 467.85,
          "end": 471.15,
          "en": "And that's exactly what response of the sign means,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
